{{root|en|ine-pro|*kʷyeh₁-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ML.|quiētus||at rest}}. {{doublet|en|quiet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kwaɪˈiːtəs/}}
* {{enPR|kwī.ēʹtəs}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# A [[stillness]] or [[pause]]; something that [[quiet]]s or [[repress]]es; removal from [[activity]].
#* {{RQ:James Bostonians|page=284|chapter=XXX|passage=Olive's specific terrors and dangers had by this time very much blown over; Basil Ransom had given no sign of life for ages, and Henry Burrage had certainly got his '''quietus''' before they went to Europe.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[death|Death]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|act=III|scene=i|page=265|passage=When he himſelfe might his '''''Quietus''''' make / With a bare Bodkin?}}
# Final [[settlement]] (e.g., of a debt).

